# Jarvis — resume rules (Cline-native, auto-loaded)

When the user asks to **resume the jarvis project** (any phrasing: "resume", "continue",
"pick up where we left off"), do these immediately and in order, without asking questions:

1. Confirm repo root is correct (`cd` is this directory).
2. Read, in order: `docs/STATUS.md`, `logs/round6-handoff.md`, `docs/deployment-lightspeed.md`,
   `docs/topology.md`, and skim `docs/system-diagram.md` + `UPGRADES.md`.
3. Verify live state: `git status`; `launchctl list | grep jarvis` (Mac local services);
   `curl -m 8 http://100.102.0.99:8766/api/health` (Lightspeed server).
4. Then proceed with the **Next actions** priority list in `docs/STATUS.md`.
5. Keep `main`/`bot` in sync (`git checkout main && git merge --ff-only bot && git push origin main && git checkout bot && git push origin bot`) and tests green (`.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider`) before finishing.

Remote agent is available: `ssh despo@100.102.0.99 'cline --cwd C:\Users\despo\jarvis --json "<task>"'` to offload heavy/Windows-native work to the Lightspeed Cline (delegate ONE task at a time).
